<Base
  title="Install the agent workspace in DeepSeek Harness — dsh-agent-plugins-market guide"
  description="Step-by-step guide: install dsh-agent-plugins-market in a DSH profile from the Web GUI or a terminal, add a Claude Code marketplace repo as a source, and install plugin suites with skills, MCP servers, hooks and slash commands."
>
  <h1>Install the agent workspace in DeepSeek Harness</h1>
  <p>
    This guide shows how to bring Claude Code, Codex, Cursor and Kimi plugin marketplaces into DeepSeek Harness (DSH) in a few minutes.
  </p>

  <h2>Prerequisites</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Node.js 22 or later, and a DSH Web profile with the skill service</li>
    <li>Git for Git sources</li>
    <li>A terminal only for the command-line install path; the Web GUI path needs none</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Step 1 — Install the plugin</h2>
  <p>Open the DSH Web GUI, then install the plugin from the sidebar:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Open <strong>Plugins</strong> in the sidebar.</li>
    <li>Press <strong>Add plugin</strong>.</li>
    <li>Type <code>dsh-agent-plugins-market</code>, then press <strong>Install</strong>.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>The same dialog accepts a GitHub repository address or a local directory path. Installing this way needs no terminal, because the npm package already contains built artifacts.</p>
  <p>With a terminal, either command works instead:</p>
  <pre><code># inside a dsh profile
pnpm add dsh-agent-plugins-market

# or via the dsh CLI
dsh plugin --profile &lt;name&gt; add dsh-agent-plugins-market

# or straight from GitHub
dsh plugin --profile &lt;name&gt; add github:Sivan757/dsh-agent-plugins-market</code></pre>
  <p>A GitHub install builds through <code>prepare</code> and needs Node.js and pnpm. The npm package does not.</p>

  <h2>Step 2 — Restart dsh and open the market</h2>
  <p>
    Restart dsh, open the Web GUI, then go to <strong>Settings → Agent Plugins</strong>.
    Older shells may expose a top-level page entry instead. The plugin also appears on the sidebar's <strong>Plugins</strong> page, where you can switch it off or remove it.
  </p>

  <h2>Step 3 — Add or refresh a marketplace source</h2>
  <p>
    The market lists one first-party source on first run. Press <strong>Refresh</strong> to fetch the suites inside it.
  </p>
  <p>
    To bring in another marketplace, add its repository URL as a source, for example a Claude Code marketplace repo with <code>.claude-plugin/marketplace.json</code>.
    Source ids are assigned automatically.
  </p>

  <h2>Step 4 — Install suites</h2>
  <p>
    Browse the card grid, open a suite for a preview of its skills, MCP servers, hooks and commands, then install it and ensure it is enabled.
    Managed checkouts live under <code>~/.dsh/agent-plugins/.sources/&lt;sourceId&gt;/</code> in the user dimension, or <code>&lt;project&gt;/.dsh/agent-plugins/.sources/&lt;sourceId&gt;/</code> in the project dimension.
  </p>

  <h2>Step 5 — Verify and use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>For a suite with skills, check the Skills tab, then type <code>/</code> in chat to find its user-invocable skills.</li>
    <li>For MCP, open MCP services and resolve connection or credential notices. Credentials and overrides are edited here; suite previews are read-only.</li>
    <li>Commands become slash entries. Role delegation through <code>subagent_run</code> uses a dynamic role catalog and requires host agents, tools, LLM and subagent services.</li>
    <li>LSP ships with the plugin — the language-server executable must be on PATH. Check LSP servers for diagnostics.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>See the <a href="https://github.com/Sivan757/dsh-agent-plugins-market/blob/main/docs/user/usage.md">usage guide</a> for host requirements and configuration.</p>

  <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>An installed plugin is not listed on the sidebar's <strong>Plugins</strong> page: restart DSH, then refresh that page.</li>
    <li>The market shows no suites after a refresh: check the source's scan notes in its card, then refresh again.</li>
    <li>Project-dimension MCP servers are not mounted, because DSH has no per-session tool scope; the project dimension covers skills and context.</li>
    <li>There is no file watcher. Local-source discovery caches results for up to 30 seconds; refresh the source to invalidate them. Project discovery has a separate five-second cache.</li>
    <li>Remote URL marketplace entries show as "remote reference" cards; add the target repo as a source to install them.</li>
  </ul>
</Base>
